  "response": "## What the scan says about connectivity\n\nTwo thresholds anchor everything below — the detector reports them in the evidence: **fan-in** p95 = 9, p99 = 10; **fan-out** p95 = 6, p99 = 11.\n\n| File | Fan-in | Fan-out | Direct / transitive importers | Other charges on the file |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/utils.ts` | **18** (1.8× p99) | 1 | 18 / 29 | God File 424L, swallowed error, 7× sync I/O |\n| `src/plugin.ts` | **10** (= p99) | 3 | 10 / 29 | `buildFinished` 103L, unprefixed booleans |\n| `src/index.ts` | 4 | **17** (1.5× p99) | 4 / 7 | God File 459L, 6× God Function |\n| `src/esbuild/index.ts` | 1 | **11** (= p99) | 1 / 7 | `runEsbuild` 237L, 38-key option bag |\n| `src/log.ts` | 9 (= p95) | 0 | 9 / **30** | 2 unprefixed booleans |\n| `src/rollup.ts` | 0 | 7 | **0 / 0** | `getRollupConfig` 122L, swallowed error |\n| `src/api-extractor.ts` | 1 | 6 (= p95) | 1 / 7 | `rollupDtsFiles` 85L, `Date.now()` |\n| `test/utils.ts` | 9 (= p95) | 0 | 9 / 9 | unbounded `Promise.all` |\n\n## Triage order\n\n**1. `src/utils.ts` — highest ripple in the repo, and safe to move.**\nFan-in 18 against a p99 cutoff of 10: nearly double the top tier, and the widest direct-importer count anywhere (18 direct, 29 transitive, blast_radius 0.46). It is also a 424-line God File (crime_00048), so those 18 importers are each pulling from a module that mixes unrelated concerns. The decisive detail is `test_gap: 0` on both the God File and the fan-in finding — this file has test coverage, which is what makes it the *first* pick rather than the scariest one. Do the split as pure moves (`fs`, temp-dir, jsonc parsing into separate modules) with `utils.ts` left as a re-export barrel, so none of the 18 importers change in the same commit. Fix `jsoncParse` swallowing its error (crime_00087, blast_radius 0.46) while you are in there — it silently returns `{}` to 18 direct consumers.\n\n**2. `src/plugin.ts` — same reach, no safety net.**\nFan-in 10 puts it exactly at the p99 cutoff, 29 transitive importers, blast_radius 0.45. What makes it second rather than fourth is the pairing with crime_00037: `buildFinished` is a 103-line class method with `test_gap: 0.75` — untested. High fan-in plus no tests is the combination where an agent edit fails silently downstream. Characterization tests on `buildFinished` first, then extract; don't restructure the module's exported surface until those tests exist.\n\n**3. `src/index.ts` — biggest comprehension load, smallest ripple.**\nFan-out 17 against a p99 of 11 — the most coupled *consumer* in the repo — but fan-in is only 4 and transitive reach is 7, so restructuring here costs almost nothing downstream. That asymmetry is why it ranks third by risk and first by return on effort.\n\nOne caveat on reading its six God Function findings: they are nested, not six separate problems. `build` 167–459 ⊃ anonymous 183–456 ⊃ `mainTasks` 260–453 ⊃ {`buildAll` 291–365, `startWatcher` 367–445}. It is one 293-line nest reported at five depths. Lifting `buildAll` and `startWatcher` to module scope collapses most of the findings at once, and `normalizeOptions` (96L, 70–165) is genuinely separate. `test_gap: 0` throughout, so this is low-risk work.\n\n**4. `src/esbuild/index.ts` — contained, and the cleanest single win.**\nFan-out 11 sits at the p99 cutoff, but fan-in is 1 and blast radius 0.25 (1 direct / 7 transitive). `runEsbuild` is 237 lines at 4.0× threshold, reading 38 distinct properties off one `options` bag (crime_00023). Nobody but its one importer can be broken by this, and `test_gap: 0` means the behaviour is pinned. Split by esbuild lifecycle stage.\n\n## Leave alone\n\n**`src/log.ts` — do not touch, despite the highest transitive reach in the repo (30).** Fan-in 9 sits at the p95 floor, fan-out is 0, and the only finding against it is crime_00014: two unprefixed booleans (`onlyImportant`, `silent`). A small, stable, zero-dependency leaf that many modules import is correct architecture — the detector is measuring popularity, not coupling debt. Renaming the booleans would touch 9 importers to satisfy a naming convention; the trade is bad.\n\n**`src/rollup.ts` — the clearest deferral.** Fan-out 7 barely clears the p95 of 6, but fan-in is 0 and `blast_radius` is literally 0 with **0 direct and 0 transitive importers**. Nothing in the scanned graph depends on it, so `getRollupConfig` (122L), the False Identity naming (crime_00004), and the swallowed error in `runRollup` are all locally contained. Real problems, zero blast-radius payoff.\n\n**`schema.json` — skip.** 362-line God File with blast_radius 0. It is a JSON schema, not a module; \"split by responsibility\" doesn't apply.\n\n**`src/api-extractor.ts` — marginal.** Fan-out 6 is exactly the p95 cutoff — the bottom of the tier, and the detector's own wording (\"appears to be in the top connectivity tier\") is hedged. Fan-in 1, blast 0.25. Fix the `Date.now()` and the swallowed error opportunistically; don't schedule a refactor.\n\n**`test/utils.ts` — expected shape.** Fan-in 9 from 9 test files is what a test harness looks like. The unbounded `Promise.all` (crime_00089) is worth a concurrency cap since it's cheap, but it's test-only.\n\n**`src/cli-main.ts` — high severity, low reach.** `main` is 153 lines (2.5× threshold, severity 0.9), but blast_radius is 0.15 with 2 transitive importers. It's a CLI entry point; extract when you're next in the file.\n\n**`src/esbuild/postcss.ts`, `svelte.ts`, `rollup/ts-resolve.ts` — same nesting artifact as `index.ts`.** `postcssPlugin` 6–145 ⊃ `setup` 18–143; `sveltePlugin` 9–124 ⊃ `setup` 17–122 ⊃ anon 31–121; `tsResolvePlugin` 28–115 ⊃ `resolveId` 37–113. Each is one plugin closure counted two or three times. All fan-in 1, transitive 7. Defer.\n\n## One caveat on the ranking\n\nEvery finding in this scan has `churn: 0` and `recency: 0` — the fixture has no usable git history, so the aggregate risk score is running on structure alone. In a real repo I'd cross-check this order against `crimes hotspots`; a file with modest fan-in that changes weekly can outrank `src/utils.ts` on expected cost. The order above is the best call available from static connectivity, and it should be re-run against history before anyone commits to a refactor sequence.",
